Z||000000||OcalaFiero||08-14-2001||11:32 AM||||I'm in the middle of a fuel pump replacement on my 86 2M4 (5 Speed) and when I got the car up on stands and slid unterneath, I found a loose wire hanging down towards the front of the engine on the driver's side. It's a medium gauge black wire with a good sized eyelit on the loose end of it. The end that is still attached is bolted to the driver's side rear strut tower and the wire is just about long enough to reach the area around the starter. The engine does crank, so it's not the starter ground. Does anyone out there have an idea of where the wire should be connected to? Thanks in advance.||||reg||9
Z||000001||fierohoho||08-14-2001||02:11 PM||||I believe it may be an engine to frame ground wire, if not it couldn't hurt. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
